Atlas overlay patch 0030: ui/privacy-button
Why: the toolbar of the reel is sidebar toggle, back, forward, reload, the omnibox, then privacy,
bookmark, downloads and the menu (reel scene R02). The privacy button and the bookmark button are
new files in the overlay tree (chrome/browser/ui/atlas/toolbar); this patch only hooks them in:
ToolbarView::Init() adds them right after the omnibox, ShowBookmarkBubble() anchors to the toolbar
bookmark button when it is shown, and the bookmark page action of the omnibox steps aside while the
pref atlas.toolbar.show_bookmark_button is on (default on), so the page has one bookmark control.
The default button set of a new profile is not changed here but by the registrar of the area
(toolbar_prefs.cc, SetDefaultPrefValue on the engine's own helium.browser.show_* prefs and the
pinned actions), so the person keeps the engine's own way of choosing buttons.
